    title_en: "Japanese Customer Service Platform Hacked: Scala Communications System Leaks Personal Data of Five Companies, Exceeding 700,000 Records",
    summary_en: "The online consultation system \"i-ask\" operated by Japanese customer service platform provider Scala Communications was subjected to unauthorized external access, resulting in the leakage of personal data belonging to multiple clients. Affected clients include Daiwa Securities, Citizen Watch, and Sompo Japan, among five other enterprises. Hackers accessed the client data database from the same server by logging into and installing software on the i-ask management website. The data leakage occurred between approximately 20:30 on October 2, 2026, and 08:00 on October 3, 2026. The compromised data includes names, email addresses, account numbers, addresses, phone numbers, and driver's license numbers, totaling over 710,000 records. Although the companies have announced that the leaked information does not include financial details such as bank account numbers, the incident highlights the security risks posed by third-party service providers and reminds customers to be vigilant against phishing scams.",
