    category: "Windows",
    title: "微軟修補 Windows 11 系統設定漏洞，阻止用戶繞過 Microsoft 帳號要求",
    summary: "本文報導指出，微軟已修補了一個允許用戶在 Windows 11 首次設定（OOBE）過程中繞過必須使用 Microsoft 帳號的漏洞。過去，如果用戶在設定流程中點擊「了解更多」的提示，系統會直接跳到只需輸入名稱和密碼的介面，從而規避了帳號驗證的必要步驟。Windows prodder Bob Pony 首次記錄了此漏洞，並報告了其已被修復。目前，雖然仍存在其他非官方的繞過方法，但這些方法已超出一般用戶的技術能力。微軟要求 Windows 11 Home 和 Pro 在初次設定時使用帳號，這與許多 Linux 發行版不強制要求帳號的做法形成對比。該漏洞據稱已在伺服器端「靜默修補」，顯示出微軟迅速修補的趨勢。",
    tags: ["Windows 11", "OOBE", "Microsoft 帳號", "微軟", "系統設定", "漏洞"],
    title_en: "Microsoft Patches Windows 11 Setup Vulnerability, Preventing Users from Bypassing Microsoft Account Requirement",
    summary_en: "This report indicates that Microsoft has patched a vulnerability that previously allowed users to bypass the requirement of using a Microsoft account during the Windows 11 Out-of-Box Experience (OOBE) setup. Previously, if a user clicked the 'Learn more' prompt during the setup process, the system would skip directly to an interface requiring only a name and password, thereby circumventing the necessary account verification steps. Windows product developer Bob Pony first documented this vulnerability and reported that it has been fixed. Although other unofficial bypass methods still exist, these methods are beyond the technical capability of the average user. Microsoft mandates the use of an account for initial setup on both Windows 11 Home and Pro, which contrasts with the practice of many Linux distributions that do not enforce account requirements. The vulnerability was reportedly 'silently patched' on the server side, demonstrating Microsoft's trend toward rapid patching.",
