    title_en: "Microsoft Windows 11 Major Feature Release: Users Focus on Performance Optimization and AI Overexposure",
    summary_en: "At a major Windows event, Microsoft announced several new features, highlighted by a brand-new Windows Search built on WinUI 3. This feature includes practical capabilities such as adjusting microphone volume, taking screenshots, arranging windows, and sending text, and is expected to launch 'later this year.' However, the focus of the event was overly concentrated on concepts like 'agent,' 'Copilot,' and 'AI.' The high frequency of these terms led users and the community to express dissatisfaction, arguing that the company overlooked essential performance fixes, stability improvements, and general quality-of-life upgrades for Windows 11. Although Microsoft has promised a series of fixes and optimizations (such as movable taskbars and skippable updates), users continue to prioritize overall system performance enhancement, especially optimization for devices with 8GB RAM, as well as fundamental improvements to core components like the Start menu and File Explorer. Overall, users desire Windows to run stably, rather than merely serving as a platform for AI applications.",
