    title_en: "Atlassian Data Center Products Face CVE-2026-21589 Arbitrary File Access Vulnerability, Exploitation Observed in the Wild",
    summary_en: "This week's cybersecurity focus is on the CVE-2026-21589 vulnerability affecting the Atlassian Data Center product suite. This arbitrary file access vulnerability (CVSS Score: 9.3) has a wide impact, affecting multiple products including Bitbucket Data Center, Confluence Data Center, Jira Service Management Data Center, Jira Software Data Center, Bamboo Data Center, Crowd Data Center, Crucible, and Fisheye. Shortly after watchTowr published technical details, attackers began exploiting this vulnerability in honeypot networks. Practical impact suggests that attackers can utilize this vulnerability to access sensitive files under specific conditions. Users are advised to monitor official Atlassian announcements immediately and apply patches or implement permission restrictions as soon as possible to mitigate the risk of exploitation. Furthermore, reports this week indicate that the China-linked APT group Flax Typhoon continues to deploy within critical infrastructure and OT systems, posing ongoing threats to national security.",
    tags_en: ["Atlassian", "CVE-2026-21589", "Data Center", "Arbitrary File Access", "APT", "Flax Typhoon"],
