    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "GitLab 警告：CI/CD 正則表達式編譯器存在最高嚴重性 RCE 漏洞 CVE-2026-97229",
    summary: "GitLab 警告用戶，其 CI/CD 正則表達式編譯器存在一個最高嚴重性的漏洞 CVE-2026-97229。此漏洞源於正則表達式編譯器中的整數溢位（integer overflow）弱點，可能允許遠端未經身份驗證的攻擊者，透過精心構造的正則表達式，在目標實例上執行任意程式碼（RCE）。該漏洞影響 GitLab Community Edition (CE) 和 Enterprise Edition (EE) 的特定版本，包括 19.2 之前、19.3 之前和 19.4 之前。GitLab 已修復此安全問題，並強烈建議所有自架設的用戶立即升級到修補版本。用戶應注意，GitLab.com 已經運行修補版本，而 GitLab Dedicated 客戶無需採取行動。此漏洞是 GitLab 近期修補的一系列漏洞之一，顯示出其平台在安全方面的持續關注。",
    tags: ["GitLab", "CVE-2026-97229", "RCE", "CI/CD", "正則表達式", "整數溢位"],
    title_en: "GitLab Alert: Critical RCE Vulnerability in CI/CD Regex Compiler (CVE-2026-97229)",
    summary_en: "GitLab warns users about a critical vulnerability, CVE-2026-97229, found in its CI/CD regular expression compiler. This flaw stems from an integer overflow weakness within the regex compiler, which could potentially allow unauthenticated remote attackers to execute arbitrary code (RCE) on a target instance using a specially crafted regular expression. The vulnerability affects specific versions of GitLab Community Edition (CE) and Enterprise Edition (EE), including versions prior to 19.2, prior to 19.3, and prior to 19.4. GitLab has patched this security issue and strongly recommends that all self-hosted users upgrade immediately to the patched version. Users should note that GitLab.com is already running the patched version, and GitLab Dedicated customers do not need to take action. This vulnerability is one of several recent patches released by GitLab, demonstrating its continued focus on platform security.",
    tags_en: ["GitLab", "CVE-2026-97229", "RCE", "CI/CD", "Regular Expression", "Integer Overflow"],
    sources: [
      { name: "BleepingComputer", url: "https://bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/gitlab-warns-of-max-severity-rce-flaw-in-regex-compiler-engine", lang: "EN" }
    ]
