    title_en: "Apple M6 MacBook Pro Expected Upgrade: Featuring Dual 16-Core Neural Engine and New Core Architecture",
    summary_en: "This article predicts that the upcoming M6 MacBook Pro from Apple will bring three major upgrades. First, the M6 chip will introduce a dual 16-core Neural Engine, offering up to double the peak computing power compared to the M5 and earlier versions, significantly boosting the execution speed of on-device AI workflows. Second, the base M6 chip will integrate three types of cores for the first time: Super cores (for single-threaded workloads), Performance cores (for complex multi-threaded workloads with lower power consumption), and Efficiency cores (for handling daily background tasks). This makes Pro-grade core performance capabilities available to standard M6 users for the first time. Furthermore, the M6 chip adopts a brand new 2nm process, which is expected to bring massive leaps in performance and power efficiency, potentially significantly improving the battery life of products like the MacBook Pro. These upgrades are expected to enhance the user experience in AI applications, multitasking, and mobile usage scenarios.",
