    summary_en: "According to Bloomberg, Epic Games is undergoing a major development strategy shift for its collaboration project with The Walt Disney Company, fully adopting an 'AI-first' development model. This model aims to have AI models write all the code and guide the generation of all art assets. Internal employee messages indicate that the role of human developers will transition to managing and guiding code and art assets generated by models like Anthropic's Claude, marking a shift toward 'no more hand-written code' and assets 'fully generated by AI workflow.' The Marvel and Star Wars themed shooter game, originally slated for a 2027 release, has been indefinitely postponed due to these AI-related adjustments and slower-than-expected development progress. Epic Games stated that this transition aims to accelerate development through AI, allowing developers to become vision and creativity drivers, with the goal of enabling the team to create more and higher-quality products.",
